{
  "reason": "The current sampled-softmax loss weights selected transitions uniformly across the batch, potentially diluting recent context and giving longer histories more influence. Macro validation HR@10 of 0.4912 versus 0.505 for the baseline, including Electronics declining from 0.420 to 0.375, motivates testing this hypothesis without establishing causality. Modify only model_design, where SASRec.ranking_loss implements the reduction; historical sampled-softmax experiments support retaining the existing network and sampling design while isolating recency weighting.",
  "module": [
    "model_design"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Replace only the loss reduction inside SASRec.ranking_loss(seq, pos, negatives, excluded), preserving its signature, existing variable names, transition selection, logits, exclusion masks, and 256-negative sampling; compute F.cross_entropy with reduction='none'. Before flattening selected transitions, compute their distances d from the final nonpadding target position in each supplied training window, rather than from the latest randomly selected transition, and retain weights 2^(-d/8) through the existing keep mask; right alignment means d = pos.shape[1] - 1 - selected. Use owner-indexed scatter_add operations in float32 to accumulate weighted losses and weights per history, divide each history's loss sum by its weight sum with a numerical safeguard, and average over histories containing valid selected targets, returning the same differentiable scalar interface. This tests whether emphasizing recent targets and balancing histories improves next-item ranking while retaining the historically useful sampled-softmax design; treat a macro HR@10 gain of 0.005–0.015 over 0.4912 as a hypothesis, assessed through the unchanged pinned host evaluator and category-level results. Explicitly retain prepared splits and preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42 and evaluation seed 42, DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], all four categories and routing, architecture, maximum history length 64, prefix augmentation, optimizer, learning-rate schedule, batching, stopping rules, SASREC_EPOCHS default 200, validation with 200 users/category and 99 unique negatives, final validation-score print, predictor writer and inference architecture, single-GPU execution and existing time limits, and trial-local artifacts; train from scratch and load exactly one selected checkpoint per category, with no ensembles, checkpoint averaging, other-trial checkpoint reuse, extra data, hidden-test access, or evaluator changes.",
    "training_evaluation": null
  }
}
